From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:34:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 084/110] Drag a tab anywhere into the other view, with
 feedback

A tab dragged from one view now drops anywhere in the other: its tab bar,
the empty space after the tabs, or its editor and preview. It goes after
the last tab there. While dragging, the target view gets an accent
outline and its tab bar a marker where the tab lands; a view where a drop
would do nothing is not highlighted. A drop in the view the tab came from
moves nothing, and a reorder in its own bar works as before.

The dragged tab is the one under the pointer as the drag starts; when the
pointer leaves the bar before it reports one, the tab shown in the view
the drag started from. Each view takes drops under a fixed id, so an offer
that entered in one frame still reaches it after the view is rebuilt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

